Subject: Open the main window maximized

The window is created at the primary monitor's full mode size, which with the
compositor's title bar is taller than the work area and puts the bottom of the
interface under the panel. Maximized, the compositor sizes it to the work area.

--- a/src/main.c
+++ b/src/main.c
@@ -390,6 +390,7 @@
     glfwWindowHint(GLFW_DOUBLEBUFFER, GLFW_TRUE);
     glfwWindowHintString(GLFW_WAYLAND_APP_ID, "goxel");
     glfwWindowHintString(GLFW_X11_CLASS_NAME, "goxel");
+    glfwWindowHint(GLFW_MAXIMIZED, GLFW_TRUE);
     monitor = glfwGetPrimaryMonitor();
     mode = glfwGetVideoMode(monitor);
     if (mode) {
